<!--
    #871: a computed value copied to a global after an aliasing pointer load
    must keep that store after the load (P6 kuna_globalorder). A switch's
    case-local copies must likewise stay on their original paths; P3
    kuna_globalorderkeep preserves them before a forced return-phi merge.
    This is a strict fix at the existing indexaliasguard global default.

    ew is GCC -O0 for `t = gi * 2 + b; x = *p; gi = t; return x + t * 100`.
    For gi=4, p=&gi, b=1 the binary returns 904; the old early store returns
    909. pick is Clang -O0 for globalorder_x86_64.c's volatile switch, whose
    stores exist only in the selected case (or default). The old output
    printed `sink = a0 & 0xffff` before the switch and read sink back in cases.
    Each assertion fails on the unfixed default tree. Native CLI tests compare
    compiler roundtrips and hardware read/write watchpoint traces as well.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1149" readonly="true">
f30f1efa554889e548897de88975e48b05b62e00008d14008b45e401d08945f8488b45e88b008945fc8b45f88905992e00008b45f86bd0648b45fc01d05dc3
</bytechunk>
